# oracle: RHEO Poiseuille flow (cut down, 400 steps, a body force of 0.01) with fix rheo interface/reconstruct: chi, the solid wall densities reconstructed from the fluid pressures (tait/water for the wall type, linear for the fluid), the corrected wall velocities and densities in pair rheo, the gradients and the shift, and fix setforce on the walls (store_forces); chi and the wall densities reduced in thermo
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-13
# fp_store is defined first with ghost yes, which compute rheo/interface then uses: the property it creates itself (fix property/atom d2_fp_store 3) has no ghost communication, so on a neighbor rebuild step native's ghosts keep the values of the slot's previous ghost until the next forward communication. Measured with native LAMMPS: without this line the run differs from step 49 (the first rebuild that changes the ghosts near x = 0; the wall densities there by 1e-3), and with it engine and native agree through step 49 to 1e-12; the engine reads the owner's value either way.
# Measured with native LAMMPS: engine vs native thermo 7.4e-10, atoms 5.8e-10.
units        lj
atom_style   rheo
dimension    2
boundary     p p p
comm_modify  vel yes

region       box block 0 12 -6 6 -0.01 0.01
create_box   2 box
lattice      sq 1.0

region       inner   block INF INF -4.5 4.5 INF INF units box
region       walls   block INF INF -4.5 4.5 INF INF units box side out

create_atoms 2 region walls
create_atoms 1 region inner

group        fluid type 1
group        rig type 2

displace_atoms fluid random 0.1 0.1 0 135414 units box

variable     rho0 equal 1.0
variable     cs equal 1.0
variable     mp equal ${rho0}/1.0
variable     zeta equal 1.0
variable     fext equal 1e-4/1.0
variable     dt_max equal  0.1*3.0/${cs}/3
variable     Dr equal 0.05*3.0*${cs}
variable     eta equal 0.1

mass         * ${mp}
set          group all rheo/rho ${rho0}
set          group all rheo/status 0
set          group rig rheo/status 1

timestep     ${dt_max}

pair_style   rheo 3.0 artificial/visc ${zeta} rho/damp ${Dr}
pair_coeff   * *

fix          fp all property/atom d2_fp_store 3 ghost yes
fix          1 all rheo 3.0 quintic 0 shift interface/reconstruct
fix          2 all rheo/viscosity * constant ${eta}
fix          3 all rheo/pressure 1 linear 2 tait/water
fix          4 rig setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
fix          5 fluid addforce 0.01 0.0 0.0
fix          6 all enforce2d

compute      rho all rheo/property/atom rho
compute      ch all rheo/property/atom chi rho
compute      chr rig reduce sum c_ch[1] c_ch[2]
compute      chf fluid reduce sum c_ch[1]

thermo       50
thermo_style custom step time ke press c_chr[*] c_chf
thermo_modify format float %.15g

run          400
